```csharp
using System;
using System.Runtime.InteropServices;

public static class NativeCompression
{
    [DllImport("compresslib", EntryPoint = "compress_buffer", CallingConvention = CallingConvention.Cdecl, ExactSpelling = true)]
    public static extern int CompressBuffer(
        [In] byte[] input,
        UIntPtr inputLen,
        [Out] byte[] output,
        UIntPtr outputLen,
        out UIntPtr bytesWritten);
}
```

`UIntPtr` is used for `size_t` since it's 4 bytes on x86 (and would scale to 8 bytes on x64 if retargeted). The `EntryPoint` ensures the managed name can follow C# conventions while matching the native symbol.
